# Coll_MoveBlockMap's ceiling hits moving up (ruling 5, 2; $012054-$01208A), at
# Stage1_SpawnGiftBox's first call (TAS f13247, the truck scene: g_LayerA holds the truck's 294x15
# block map, the one of TAS RAM dump f13500), each case an airborne mover's call as
# Coll_MoveAirborneBlockMap makes it (d1/d2 the move, d4/d5 the position, d6/d7 the masks: moving up
# only bit 0 counts, so 1). The positions are the map's own ceilings (scratchpad cov17_ceil.py).
# Reachability undetermined (NOTES, Open questions: cov13's "Coll_MoveBlockMap / Coll_WalkBlockMap":
# the ceiling hit ran once in the TAS, never at a block-row boundary, with x steps left; not
# judged): a mover jumping into these ceilings from below is not excluded by anything known.
at $020792

# The hit at a block-row boundary ($012054-$01207A): the 1-px wall in column 0 of block (90,11)
# (cell $0408, mask 1, span 00-0F) ends at y 191 with block (90,12) open below; a mover at
# (1440, 192) moving straight up 2 px hits its bottom pixel, row 15 of the block above, and is put
# back at row 0 of its own block.
case boundary_hit
reg d1 = 0
reg d2 = -2
reg d4 = 1440
reg d5 = 192
reg d6 = 1
reg d7 = 1

# The hit with x steps left, moving left ($01207C-$01208A, on into Coll_WalkBlockMapLeft): the
# 1-px platform at row 7 of blocks (239,7)-(246,7) (y 119; cells $0010-$0028, mask 1); a mover at
# (3880, 120) moving up 6 and left 2 hits it on its first (major, y) step with both x steps to go.
case hit_moving_left
reg d1 = -2
reg d2 = -6
reg d4 = 3880
reg d5 = 120
reg d6 = 1
reg d7 = 1
